From 4946e574cc5c320e4450cf70b60af2cd5e18f5dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tong <zhengtong0611@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:39:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] Referee: speech bridge, dance player fixes, CLI dance
 export and build

- Assets/MATE ENGINE - Referee: long-polls the debate server's
  /face/mate/next (wire protocol v1) and shows the referee's line in a
  speech bubble with the mouth moving while the voice plays. Off unless
  -speech-bridge <url>, MEX_SPEECH_BRIDGE or speech_bridge.json is set.
  Booted by RuntimeInitializeOnLoadMethod, no scene edits.
- AvatarDancePlayer: logs the dance scan, the chosen clip/audio and why
  a dance didn't play; leaves the waiting pose on failure; never picks a
  controller-less helper Animator (ADS_ProxyRoot) as the avatar, which
  made every dance fail silently once the avatar had been hidden by the
  first-run tutorial.
- DanceModCli / RefereeBuild / build-referee.sh: export dance mods and
  build the Linux player from the command line.
- --dance-autoplay test hook, tools/mock_mate_server.py.
